    "homeType": "MULTI_FAMILY",
    "description": "This well-maintained 4-unit building at 476 7th Avenue is ideally located in San Franciscos Inner Richmond District, between Geary Boulevard and Anza Street, just steps from the Kaiser Permanente French Campus and a variety of popular restaurants and shops. Built in 1971, the property offers 4,054 Sqft of living space on a nearly 3,000 Sqft lot, with two units that are 3bed/2bath and two units that are 2bed/1bath. The building features a spacious 34 car garage with a refurbished door and new controller, plus other recent upgrades including double-insulated windows, a new roof, updated electrical panel, stair lift, and a modern intercom system. Right now, 3 of the 4 units are currently occupied, with one vacant unit. A prime Inner Richmond investment opportunity, close to abundant shopping, dining, and amenities. This property presents excellent income potential, offering the flexibility to live in one unit while renting out the others, or to accommodate multi-generational living under one roof. Dont miss this rare chance to own a versatile property in a prime San Francisco neighborhood."
  },
